<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32372" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">offensus</span></b> , ūs, m.
		1. offendo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a striking against</i>, <i>a
			shock</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-class. prose).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 2,
			223</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 359</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4,
			39</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<i>A lighting upon</i>, <i>meeting
			with</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per offensus armorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 12, 283</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>An offence</i>, <i>vexation</i>, <i>annoyance</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sin vita in offensu est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					3, 941</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>